<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   AgentPro: nothing this app stores may leave the device.

   Android's auto-backup is on by default and copies the whole sandbox to the user's Google
   Drive. That sandbox holds linphonerc - which carries the SIP account's password in clear -
   plus the call history, the chat database and the PBX settings. So the credentials of every
   agent would sit in Google's storage, survive an uninstall, and restore themselves onto any
   new phone signed in to the same account. That is a wider exposure than anything left on the
   device itself, and it happens with no action from the user.

   This file governs Android 11 and below. res/xml/data_extraction_rules.xml governs 12+, and
   android:allowBackup="false" in the manifest is what actually switches the feature off - the
   rules here are the belt to that pair of braces, so a future build that flips allowBackup
   back on does not silently start shipping accounts to the cloud.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="root" path="." />
    <exclude domain="file" path="." />
    <exclude domain="database" path="." />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
    <exclude domain="external" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
